# Field table: Japannext PTS GLIMPSE snapshot service, in two layers.
#
# Session layer: Japannext SoupBinTCP Specification (All Markets), version 1.01, last
# updated January 16, 2026 (JNX SoupBinTCP 1.01). Its tables put the 2-byte Packet
# Length at offset 0 and the Packet Type at offset 2. Here the length is the
# @length_prefix (it excludes itself: "number of bytes after this field until next
# packet") and every offset is the table's offset minus 2. The same layer carries ITCH
# over TCP (itch.tbl).
#
# Application layer: GLIMPSE Market Data Specification (Equities), version 2.01, last
# updated January 16, 2026 (JNX GLIMPSE 2.01): the payload of each Sequenced Data
# Packet, without a length prefix. The specification does not state message totals;
# each @size is the last row's offset plus its length.
@venue jnx
@endian big
@pad space
@type Integer uint
@type Alpha char
@type Alphanumeric char
# JNX SoupBinTCP 1.01 5.2.1 and 5.3.1: Session, Requested Session and the Numeric
# sequence numbers are left-padded with spaces (right-aligned).
@type Session char right
@type Numeric char right
@type Payload bytes

### soup::from_jnx
@length_prefix 2 exclusive

MessageType + 0 1 # DebugPacket: human-readable text; either side may send it at any time (JNX SoupBinTCP 1.01, 5.1, p. 5)
Text Payload 1 # Human-readable text

MessageType A 0 1 # LoginAcceptedPacket: login succeeded; first non-debug packet after it (5.2.1, p. 5)
@size 31
Session Session 1 10 # Session ID of the current session, left-padded with spaces
SequenceNumber Numeric 11 20 # Sequence number (ASCII) of the next Sequenced Message, left-padded with spaces

MessageType J 0 1 # LoginRejectedPacket: login failed; the server then closes the socket (5.2.2, p. 5-6)
@size 2
RejectReasonCode Alpha 1 1 # A not authorized (username, password, or username and port do not match), S session not available (Table 1)

MessageType S 0 1 # SequencedDataPacket: one sequenced message of the higher-level protocol (5.2.3, p. 6)
Message Payload 1 # GLIMPSE or ITCH message

MessageType H 0 1 # ServerHeartbeatPacket: sent after more than 1 second without other data (5.2.4, p. 6)
@size 1

MessageType Z 0 1 # EndOfSessionPacket: no more messages; the connection is then closed (5.2.5, p. 6)
@size 1

### soup::to_jnx
@length_prefix 2 exclusive

MessageType + 0 1 # DebugPacket: human-readable text (5.1, p. 5)
Text Payload 1 # Human-readable text

MessageType L 0 1 # LoginRequestPacket: first packet after connecting; the server may drop the connection after about 30 seconds without it (5.3.1, p. 7)
@size 47
Username Alphanumeric 1 6 # Case-sensitive, right-padded with spaces
Password Alphanumeric 7 10 # Case-sensitive, right-padded with spaces
RequestedSession Session 17 10 # Session to log in to, blank for the current one, left-padded with spaces; GLIMPSE requires it blank (JNX GLIMPSE 2.01, 4)
RequestedSequenceNumber Numeric 27 20 # Sequence number (ASCII) of the next message wanted, 0 for the most recent, left-padded with spaces

MessageType U 0 1 # UnsequencedDataPacket: one client message of the higher-level protocol (5.3.2, p. 7)
Message Payload 1 # Higher-level protocol message

MessageType R 0 1 # ClientHeartbeatPacket: sent after more than 1 second without other data (5.3.3, p. 7)
@size 1

MessageType O 0 1 # LogoutRequestPacket: the server then closes the connection (5.3.4, p. 8)
@size 1

### glimpse::from_jnx

MessageType T 0 1 # TimestampSecondsMessage: seconds part of the timestamp (JNX GLIMPSE 2.01, 5.1, p. 4)
@size 5
TimestampSeconds Integer 1 4 # Seconds past midnight of the day the trading session started

MessageType S 0 1 # SystemEventMessage: only the Start of Messages and End of Messages events that occurred before the snapshot (5.2, p. 4)
@size 10
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
Group Alpha 5 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU; blank if system-wide
SystemEvent Alpha 9 1 # O start of messages, C end of messages (Table 1)

MessageType L 0 1 # PriceTickSizeMessage: one row of a price tick size table; sent before Orderbook Directory Messages (5.3, p. 5)
@size 17
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
PriceTickSizeTableId Integer 5 4 # Price tick size table identifier
PriceTickSize Integer 9 4 # Price tick size
PriceStart Integer 13 4 # Start of the price range for this tick size

MessageType R 0 1 # OrderbookDirectoryMessage: an order book available for trading (5.4, p. 5)
@size 45
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderbookId Alpha 5 4 # SICC code
OrderbookCode Alpha 9 12 # ISIN
Group Alpha 21 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
RoundLotSize Integer 25 4 # Shares in a round lot
PriceTickSizeTableId Integer 29 4 # Price tick size table identifier
PriceDecimals Integer 33 4 # Decimal places in price fields; value is 1
UpperPriceLimit Integer 37 4 # Maximum tradable price
LowerPriceLimit Integer 41 4 # Minimum tradable price

MessageType H 0 1 # TradingStateMessage: sent for every order book eligible for trading at the snapshot; a book without one is suspended (5.5, p. 6)
@size 14
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderbookId Alpha 5 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 9 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
TradingState Alpha 13 1 # T trading, V suspended

MessageType Y 0 1 # ShortSellingPriceRestrictionStateMessage: sent for every order book with a restriction in effect at the snapshot (5.6, p. 6)
@size 14
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderbookId Alpha 5 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 9 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
ShortSellingState Alpha 13 1 # 0 no price restriction, 1 price restriction in effect

MessageType A 0 1 # OrderAddedMessage: Order Added Message - No Attributes; an order present in the displayable book, or a reference price when Order Number is 0 (5.7.1, p. 7)
@size 30
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order number, unique per day per order book group; 0 is a reference price message
BuySellIndicator Alpha 13 1 # B buy, S sell; ignore if reference price message
Quantity Integer 14 4 # Shares; ignore if reference price message
OrderbookId Alpha 18 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 22 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
Price Integer 26 4 # Order price, 1 decimal place; reference price message: 0x7FFFFFFF means none available

MessageType F 0 1 # OrderAddedWithAttributesMessage: an order with market-specific attributes present in the displayable book (5.7.2, p. 8)
@size 35
TimestampNanoseconds Integer 1 4 # Nanoseconds since the last Timestamp - Seconds Message
OrderNumber Integer 5 8 # Order number, unique per day per order book group
BuySellIndicator Alpha 13 1 # B buy, S sell
Quantity Integer 14 4 # Shares
OrderbookId Alpha 18 4 # SICC code
Group Alpha 22 4 # Order book group: DAY, NGHT, DAYX, DAYU
Price Integer 26 4 # Order price, 1 decimal place
Attribution Alpha 30 4 # Reserved, always blank
OrderType Alpha 34 1 # Q DLP order

MessageType G 0 1 # EndOfSnapshotMessage: last message of the snapshot; the ITCH sequence number to resume the real-time feed from (5.8, p. 8)
@size 9
SequenceNumber Integer 1 8 # ITCH market data feed sequence number

### end
